QA|What is a confidence interval?|A confidence interval is produced by a procedure that, under its assumptions and repeated sampling, covers the fixed parameter at a stated long-run frequency.|synthetic-gpt6-en-v1
QA|What is Bayesian inference?|Bayesian inference updates a probability distribution over hypotheses or parameters by combining prior information with observed data through Bayes' theorem.|synthetic-gpt6-en-v1
QA|What is entropy in information theory?|Shannon entropy measures the expected information content or uncertainty of a discrete random variable, based on its probability distribution.|synthetic-gpt6-en-v1
