QA|What is lossy compression?|Lossy compression reduces data size by discarding information judged less important, so exact reconstruction is generally impossible.|synthetic-gpt6-en-v1
QA|What is Unicode?|Unicode is a standard that assigns code points to characters and defines properties and algorithms for representing text across writing systems.|synthetic-gpt6-en-v1
QA|What is UTF-8?|UTF-8 is a variable-length Unicode encoding that represents code points using one to four bytes and is compatible with ASCII for the first 128 code points.|synthetic-gpt6-en-v1
QA|What is normalization in Unicode text?|Unicode normalization transforms equivalent sequences into standardized forms such as NFC or NFD, which can improve consistent comparison while preserving text meaning.|synthetic-gpt6-en-v1
